# ============================================================
# ITM Server Security Monitor
# Command-and-control watchlist
#
# Installed to /etc/security-monitor/known-c2.list
#
# Deliberately a separate, dead simple file: one indicator per
# line, no syntax, no types. Adding an address during an
# incident must not require editing source code or knowing the
# IOC database format.
#
#   1.2.3.4              IPv4
#   2001:db8::1          IPv6
#   evil.example         domain (also matches subdomains)
#
# Checked against:
#   - established sockets  (ss, resolved from a trusted path)
#   - the resolver configuration and /etc/hosts
#   - DNS resolution of the listed domains, so a host that can
#     still reach the C2 is reported even with no live session
#
# Entries are labelled by technique, not by the host they came
# from: this file is deployed fleet-wide, and which server a
# match occurred on is recorded in the finding itself.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. The installer merges new
# entries on upgrade and never removes yours.
# ============================================================

# --- INCIDENT: PAM credential harvester (2026-08) ---
# Collector that received the captured credentials.
